."},{"type":"h","text":"OLTP"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand transactional systems:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Orders"},{"text":"Payments"},{"text":"Customers"},{"text":"Products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"OLAP"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand analytical systems:"}]},{"heading":"Data Warehouse Concepts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Star schema"},{"text":"Snowflake schema"},{"text":"Fact tables"},{"text":"Dimension tables"},{"text":"Slowly Changing Dimensions"},{"text":"Surrogate keys"},{"text":"A good Data Engineer should understand why data is modeled a certain way, not simply how to write SQL."}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2–3 — ETL & ELT","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the complete pipeline:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Source Systems","Extract","Ingest","Transform","Validate","Store","Serve","Analytics / AI Applications"]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ETL"},{"text":"ELT"},{"text":"Batch processing"},{"text":"Incremental loading"},{"text":"Full loads"},{"text":"Change Data Capture fundamentals"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Error handling"}]}]},{"heading":"Python for Data Engineering","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Use Python to build real pipelines."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"requests"},{"text":"SQLAlchemy"},{"text":"PyArrow"},{"text":"pathlib"},{"text":"logging"},{"text":"multiprocessing/concurrency basics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build scripts that:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Extract API data"},{"text":"Read CSV/JSON"},{"text":"Clean data"},{"text":"Transform records"},{"text":"Load databases"},{"text":"Handle failures"},{"text":"Generate logs"},{"text":"The student should move beyond notebook-based analysis toward production-style Python applications."}]}]},{"heading":"APIs & Data Ingestion","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand how modern systems ex